  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 8,
        "rationale": "The spec filters an `li` card by its entry link for the chosen post stem, mocks the GitHub pulls endpoint with an open PR whose head ref is cms/posts/<stem>, and asserts the 'preview draft' link's href equals https://preview-pr4242.<CMS_APEX>/blog/<slug>/ plus target=_blank. The post is chosen only if its front matter has published: true, which matches the Published-ON case. The state is established through a mocked GitHub path layered on a real Decap local-backend login, not a bare href check. Gaps: the Published-OFF span branch is not exercised, the preview host pattern and slug derivation (stem minus date, not title) are assumed rather than verified against posts-list-enhance.js, and the spec could not be executed because ./public-content is absent in this tree."
      },
      {
        "name": "Routing",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Tagged @admin-read with no Decap Save, no project-name skip, so both admin browser projects can run it. The posts guard uses cap.keepsBaseCollection(SITE_ROOT, 'posts') with the module-scope _posts read guarded by existsSync. Navigation uses a baseURL-relative goto and clicks the Posts link; it never opens an entry editor, so the entry-to-entry publish trap is avoided. Minor: the token seeding via localStorage is a reasonable but unverified assumption about how the dashboard gates its fetch."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "The cached diff adds exactly one new file, e2e/cms-posts-list-preview-link.spec.js. No harness, base, capability, or example spec was touched, and nothing was added to PLATFORM_META_SPECS."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply states up front that the test was not run in a browser because Playwright is absent, lists exactly what ran (check-spec in all seven modes, node --check, and a mutation check that the AST validators can fail), and clearly separates AST validation from a browser run. It also flags that ./public-content is missing so the spec cannot load locally, that it will likely skip in the bare platform, and that the gitleaks allowlist was unverified. No unsupported pass claim. Slightly short of perfect because it does not note that the preview host pattern and slug source were assumed rather than checked against the dashboard script."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 8.8
  },
